 "notes": "Restraint-only. Web browser 165->12: engine-covering market browsers per brief plus Samsung Browser, DuckDuckGo and Tor as notable privacy/mobile ones, with Internet Explorer and Netscape Navigator kept as icons of the kind; engine, privacy, mobile and AI browser are types. Dropped forks, regional browsers, minor and historic tails (Mosaic, WorldWideWeb, Lynx and other historic browsers belong on the Classic software shelf if wanted). Email client 58->12 (Eudora kept as icon; dropped server webmail RoundCube/SquirrelMail/IMP, enterprise groupware HCL Notes/GroupWise/FirstClass/Zimbra, superseded Microsoft and Netscape mail apps and minor tails; Microsoft Office range dropped). Download manager 14->8. BitTorrent client 20->12: LimeWire, FrostWire, Shareaza and MLDonkey are multi-network P2P clients (Classic software: Peer-to-peer file sharing client), minor clients dropped. No new kinds."
